 "about": "Biconical antennas solved as bodies of revolution by otahub.num.bor. Each cone truncated at a top diameter 2% of its base diameter, the two top faces 0.6 x that diameter apart, a feed tube of the top radius across the gap; a conical monopole on an infinite plane is half of it (image theory): half the impedance, twice the directivity, gap 0.3 x top diameter. th = half angle (deg); k = slant/lambda at the cutoff, where VSWR first falls to 2 and stays there - against the characteristic impedance for 'bic', 50 ohm for 'mono' - extrapolated from 24 and 48 segments per slant; band = continuous VSWR<2 f_high/f_low (10 where it ran past a decade); worst = highest VSWR from 2 to 10 x f_low; D = peak directivity at the cutoff. Monopole rows at 32-34 degrees resolve a steep threshold: their band and worst are interpolated from 30 and 35, both of which hold a decade.",
